{number: 66}
{title: Out of My Bondage, Sorrow, and Night}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Out of my bondage, sorrow and night,
Jesus, I [G7] come, Jesus, I [C] come;
Into Thy freedom, gladness and light,
Jesus, I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
Out of my [F] sickness into Thy [C] health,
Out of my [F] want and into Thy [C] wealth,
Out of my [F] sin and into Thy-[C] self,
Jesus, I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Out of my shameful failure and loss,
Jesus, I [G7] come, Jesus, I [C] come;
Into the glorious gain of Thy cross,
Jesus, I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
Out of earth's [F] sorrows into Thy [C] balm,
Out of life's [F] storms and into Thy [C] calm,
Out of dis-[F] tress to jubilant [C] psalm,
Jesus, I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Out of unrest and arrogant pride,
Jesus, I [G7] come, Jesus, I [C] come;
Into Thy blessed will to abide,
Jesus, I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
Out of my-[F] self to dwell in Thy [C] love,
Out of de-[F] spair into raptures a-[C] bove,
Upward for [F] aye on wings like a [C] dove,
Jesus, I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
